          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The usual notion of equality in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate+logic+over+type+theory"} predicate logic over type theory
            and in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
          %p
            Propositional equality is most commonly used in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theories"} set theories
            like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependently+sorted+set+theories"} dependently sorted set theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set-level+type+theories"} set-level type theories
            where all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
          %p
            Propositional equality can be contrasted with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#typed_firstorder_logic Typed first-order logic
          %p
            In any two-layer type theory with a layer of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            and a layer of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+logic"} first order logic
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has a binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            according to which two elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are related if and only if they are equal; in this case we write
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A y
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"} propositional equality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi x
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A, y:A \vdash x =_A y \; \mathrm{prop}} \quad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash x =_A x \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p Then we have the elimination rules for propositional equality:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo .
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo .
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo .
                        %mi x
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                        %mi y
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:A, y:A \vdash P(x, y) \; \mathrm{prop}}{\Gamma \vdash \left(\forall x:A.P(x, x)\right) \implies \left(\forall x:A.\forall y:A.x =_A y \implies P(x, y)\right) \; \mathrm{true}}
          %h3#untyped_firstorder_logic Untyped first-order logic
          %p
            Something similar occurs in untyped
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+logic"} first-order logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+of+discourse"} domain of discourse
            has a binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            according to which two elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            are related if and only if they are equal; in this case we write
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"} propositional equality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi y
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash x \quad \Gamma \vdash y}{\Gamma \vdash x = y \; \mathrm{prop}} \quad \frac{\Gamma \vdash x}{\Gamma \vdash x = x \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p Then we have the elimination rules for propositional equality:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                        %mo .
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                        %mo .
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi y
                        %mo .
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, x, y \vdash P(x, y) \; \mathrm{prop}}{\Gamma \vdash \left(\forall x.P(x, x)\right) \implies \left(\forall x.\forall y.x = y \implies P(x, y)\right) \; \mathrm{true}}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#propositional_equality_is_an_equivalence_relation Propositional equality is an equivalence relation
          %p The introduction rule of propositional equality says that propositional equality is reflexive.
          %p
            We can show that propositional equality is symmetric, that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y =_A x
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A x
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y =_A x
          %p
            We can also show that propositional equality is transitive, that for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z:A
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
