          %h2#propositional_equality_internal_to_a_set_theory Propositional equality internal to a set theory
          %p
            Relations and propositional equality could be
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic+of+set+theory"} internalized in any set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive relation
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            that is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
            (although that fact is somewhat circular). This relation is often called the
            %strong identity relation
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of relations.
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of reflexive relations on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality+relation"} equality relation
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is an
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial reflexive relation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+family"} type family
            instead of a family of propositions, then the equality relation is the initial type generated by reflexivity or the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+law+of+thought"} first law of thought
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times S
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            and written
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_S
            or similarly. As an abstract set, this subset is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            itself, so one also sees the diagonal as a map, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+function"} diagonal function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi S
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \overset{\Delta_S}\to S \times S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
